  "id": "COMPOUND:36563 - PROTEIN:5032",
  "verbalization": "Astragaloside a em leader pound is implicated in the biological pathway leading to DMS-79 through multiple interconnected targets. The evidence suggests that Astragaloside a em leader pound acts as a target for CD70 antigen, which in turn is targeted by a complex lipid molecule. This lipid molecule, in turn, has a direct target of DMS-79. The integration of these relationships highlights a potential mechanism where Astragaloside a em leader pound serves as a bridge, connecting to CD70 antigen, which is then targeted by a lipid compound that ultimately affects DMS-79. The presence of multiple pathways converging on DMS-79 underscores the complexity of the biological network, with Astragaloside a em leader pound playing a central role in this cascade. The evidence supports a mechanism where the compound interacts with CD70 antigen, which is then modulated by a lipid, ultimately influencing DMS-79. This suggests a possible role in signaling or metabolic pathways that are not yet fully characterized.",
